# The infinity tour: a figure-8 -- two circles joined at a point on their
# circumferences, driven as ARCS, then repeated.
#
# WHY ARCS. Each quarter circle is ONE move with a body distance AND a
# rotation, which the motion engine shapes end to end. The alternative --
# chopping a circle into dozens of straight chords -- would put an accel
# ramp and an end taper inside every chord, so the robot would stutter
# through a polygon instead of driving a curve.
#
#   TWIST vx=<v> omega=<w> angle=<a>   is an arc of radius r = v / w
#
# Four arcs of 90 deg make one circle; the second circle is driven with
# omega negated, so the robot leaves the crossing point curving the other
# way and traces the second lobe. The two lobes meet at the start point,
# which is the crossing of the 8.
#
# SIZING. r = 300 mm. A figure-8 of radius r spans 4r x 2r = 1200 x 600 mm.
# The playfield limit for the robot centre is +-671.5 x +-446.5 mm
# (1343 x 893 mm), so 1200 x 600 leaves ~71 mm of margin on x and ~146 mm
# on y. The stakeholder asked for "about 35 cm"; r = 350 would span
# 1400 mm and NOT fit (1400 > 1343), so 300 is the largest round radius
# that clears the rails. Start at the field centre facing East.
#
#   v = omega * r, with omega = 45 deg/s = 0.7854 rad/s
#   -> v = 0.7854 * 300 = 236 mm/s.
#
# SEGMENT SIZE IS NOT FREE. moveX() splits any move with a nonzero
# distance and |rotation| >= 50 deg (kTurnFirstAngleRad) into a pivot
# THEN a straight -- so 90 deg arcs come out as a SQUARE, which is
# exactly what the first run of this tour drew. Each arc must therefore
# stay under 50 deg: 45 deg gives 8 arcs per circle, still a handful of
# shaped moves rather than dozens of chords.

SET twist_hold_gain 8
SET speed_floor 512
SET yaw_taper 800
SET pivot_overrun 0.68

# --- lobe A: one full circle, CCW (omega positive) -------------------
REPEAT 8

MARK lobeA
TWIST vx=236 omega=45 angle=45 timeout=6

END

# --- lobe B: one full circle, CW (omega negative) --------------------
REPEAT 8

MARK lobeB
TWIST vx=236 omega=-45 angle=-45 timeout=6

END

STOP dwell=0.5
